### Environment Variables Example
## Uses http-client.env.json in this folder (keys: dev, prod, staging).
## activeEnv defaults to "dev".
##
## In Zed (▶ menu on the request):
##   ▶ Send Request              — send with current activeEnv
##   🌐 Switch Environment       — change activeEnv only (no send)
##   🌐 Send with Environment…   — pick env, then send
##   ⊕ Send in New Tab           — send in a new terminal tab
##
## CLI:
##   httpyac-run environments.http 9
##   httpyac-run environments.http --switch-env
##   httpyac-run environments.http 9 --env prod
##   httpyac-run environments.http 9 --pick-env

### GET using base_url from env
GET {{base_url}}/get
Accept: application/json
Host: {{api}}

### GET with api_key from env
GET {{api_url}}/headers
X-Api-Key: {{api_key}}

Accept: application/json

### POST with auth_token from env
{{
  //pre request script
  const crypto = require('crypto');
  const date = new Date();
  const signatureBase64 = crypto.createHmac('sha256', 'secret')
  .update(`${request.method}\u2028${request.url}\u2028${date.getTime()}`).digest("base64");
  exports.authDate = date.toUTCString();
  exports.authentication = `Basic ${signatureBase64}`;
}}
POST {{api_url}}/post
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
Content-Type: application/json


{
  "user": "{{user}}",
  "message": "Hello from {{base_url}}"
}

### Mix file variable with env
@endpoint = /anything

GET {{base_url}}{{endpoint}}
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}
